# L §4.5 (round 12): known in a window that holds the cut, "an as-known read ... states a windows clause or is
# HOLE-IMPRECISE (windows earliest takes the version as known on the window's first day, windows latest on its last).
# This holds for everything the version or row brings: ... its observations". st (known in window(2026-03-01,
# 2026-03-10)) covers konto in February and holds a 30.00 PLN payment out on 2026-02-10. As known 2026-03-05: a hole (q1);
# windows earliest books it: 100.00 - 30.00 = 70.00 PLN (q2); windows latest doesn't: 100.00 PLN (q3); as known
# 2026-03-15: 70.00 PLN (q4). (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.5, writer 5's T-33.)
# (Writer 8: windows earliest and latest are gone; windows each splits the line at the day the version becomes
# known, the window's days up to the cut (seen) and after it (unseen), L §4.4 "That holds for every window ...: a
# version's known (§4.5)". The earliest line is the first part, the latest the second.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 100.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version st
  cite s
  governs 2026-02
  known window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10)
  covers konto
  bank[r1] = (on: 2026-02-10, kind: transfers, leg cash from konto to world amount 30.00 PLN) "l1"

ask q1: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) as known 2026-03-05
ask q2: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) as known 2026-03-05 windows each
ask q4: bal(konto, 2026-02-28) as known 2026-03-15
=== expect
q1: ? ...
  cut 2026-03-05
q2 [known of st = 2026-03-01 .. 2026-03-05]: 70.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-05
q2 [known of st = 2026-03-06 .. 2026-03-10]: 100.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-05
q4: 70.00 PLN
  cut 2026-03-15
